{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 44, :comments ["<b>He and Hoshea son of Nun.</b> It was the Sabbath of the translator [deputy speaker]; authority was taken from this one and given to that one. Moshe set up a translator for Yehoshua, that he [Yehoshua] would expound [the Torah] during his [Moshe's] lifetime — so that Israel should not say to him, 'In your master's lifetime you had no right to lift your head.' And why does he call him here Hoshea? To tell that his mind was not haughty over him [i.e., himself]: that even though greatness was given him, he humbled himself as at the beginning (see Sifrei)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:49:29.987734668Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}